From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:43:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: End the trailing polls only after
 compute by default

With g16_tail_cut at 1, every evented pass that retired a flight ends
its trailing 5 us polls and publishes at once. That is what compute
wants: the freed unit takes the next command immediately. For render
the early publish finds nothing new, because render jobs reach the
engine only as earlier fences signal at the end of the pass, while the
trailing polls it gave up would have caught the group's second report.

On the installed kernel, switching between 1 and 2 at runtime
(1 / 2 / 1 / 2 / 1) left compute.light at depth 64 unchanged (37.8,
38.2, 37.8 against 37.8, 37.7 us per submit) and gave render.light at
depth 64 87.5, 87.3, 87.7 against 86.5, 87.0 us.

Make 2 the default. 1 and 0 remain available at runtime.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
index 823f5968e2..4644f9055b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
@@ -2039,8 +2039,8 @@ fn render_patch_parse_u32(text: &str) -> Option<u32> {
         },
     });
 
-/// Storage of `g16_tail_cut` (runtime 0644, default 1).
-static TAIL_CUT: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(1);
+/// Storage of `g16_tail_cut` (runtime 0644, default 2).
+static TAIL_CUT: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(2);
 
 /// Whether a pass woken by a firmware event ends its four trailing 5 us busy polls as soon as
 /// it has retired a flight, so that the same pass publishes into the freed unit at once. The
@@ -2050,7 +2050,7 @@ pub(crate) fn tail_cut() -> bool {
 }
 
 /// `g16_tail_cut` value: 1 every evented pass that retired a flight ends its trailing polls;
-/// 2 only a pass that retired a compute flight does. Render jobs reach the engine only as
+/// 2 (default) only one that retired a compute flight does. Render jobs reach the engine only as
 /// earlier fences signal, at the end of the pass, so for render the early publish has
 /// nothing new to publish while the trailing polls catch the group's second report.
 pub(crate) fn tail_cut_value() -> u32 {
@@ -2063,7 +2063,7 @@ pub(crate) fn tail_cut_value() -> u32 {
     TAIL_CUT_PARM,
     TAIL_CUT,
     "g16_tail_cut",
-    "G16: 1: an evented pass that retired a flight skips its remaining trailing 5 us polls and publishes at once; 2: only a pass that retired a compute flight does (default 1; 0: as before; runtime 0644)"
+    "G16: 1: an evented pass that retired a flight skips its remaining trailing 5 us polls and publishes at once; 2, the default: only a pass that retired a compute flight does (0: as before; runtime 0644)"
 );
 
 /// Storage of `g16_idle_decay` (runtime 0644, default 0).
-- 
